'''water-vacuole''' (wâ′tėr-vak″ū-ōl), ''n.'' One of the temporary vacuoles of many protozoans, consisting of a globule of water taken in with a particle of food. {{smaller|The circulation of these food-vacuoles or temporary stomachs represents a water-vascular system of the most primitive kind. See ''water-vascular''.}}

'''water-varnish''' (wâ′tėr-vär″nish), ''n.'' A varnish made by using water as a solvent.—'''Lac water-varnish.''' {{smaller|See ''lac''<sup>2</sup>.}}

'''water-vascular''' (wâ′tėr-vas″kū-lä̤r), ''a.'' In ''biol.'', pertaining to or providing for circulation of water in the body of an animal. {{smaller|The water-vascular system is seen in its utmost simplicity in infusorians, and in various degrees of complexity in higher inver-}}
