{{right|''Davies'', Muse’s Sacrifice, p. 10. (''Davies.'')}}}}

'''water-weed''' (wâ′tėr-wēd), ''n.'' '''1.''' Any wild aquatic plant without special use or beauty.
{{smaller block|<poem>The willful ''water-weeds'' held me thrall.</poem>
{{right|''S. Lanier'', The Century, XXVII. 819.}}}}

'''2.''' Specifically, the choke-pondweed or water-thyme, ''Elodea Canadensis'' (''Anacharis Alsinastrum''), of the ''Hydrocharideæ''. See ''pondweed'' and ''Babington’s-curse''.

